---
const sides = [
  {
    role: "If you built an agent",
    tint: "text-accent",
    steps: [
      { k: "01", t: "List it", d: "Paste the URL of an endpoint you already run, set a price, and give your Hedera account." },
      { k: "02", t: "Get paid", d: "The marketplace fronts your endpoint with a paywall. HBAR lands in your account, not ours." },
    ],
  },
  {
    role: "If you need an agent",
    tint: "text-text",
    steps: [
      { k: "03", t: "Discover", d: "Your agent reads the registry and picks the capability it needs, at the price it's willing to pay." },
      { k: "04", t: "Pay per call", d: "402 → sign → 200. No account, no API key, no subscription. Just the call you made." },
    ],
  },
];
---
<section id="how" class="border-t border-border/60">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 class="max-w-[22ch] text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tighter md:text-4xl">
      Two sides, and neither one signs up.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-muted">
      Sellers write no payment code. Buyers create no account. The protocol handles both ends.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {sides.map((side) => (
        <div>
          <h3 class:list={["font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.18em]", side.tint]}>{side.role}</h3>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-border">
            {side.steps.map((s) => (
              <div class="reveal bg-bg p-6">
                <div class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">{s.k}</div>
                <div class="mt-3 text-lg font-medium">{s.t}</div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{s.d}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-faint">
      The marketplace never holds seller funds — payment routes to each seller's own Hedera
      account. The facilitator covers the network fee, so sellers pay no gas.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
